  "body": "Stacked on #1144 (on #1139, #1123, #560, #551). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\nWire EDM no-core burnout (#540, part of #290): a Wire Contour with a burnout clearance burns a closed pocket's whole interior away, so no core is left to drop.\n\n- **motion** `wire_edm/burnout.rs` (new): `wire_burnout` - offset rings of the pocket from the stated wall clearance inward, 0.9 x the kerf offset apart, cut innermost first from one threading at the start hole (straight lead in, straight links ring to ring, straight lead back). Refused by name: clearance below the kerf offset (`clearance_door`, shared with the command door), no start hole, a start hole outside the clearance, the punch side, a pocket too small, a ring pattern that splits into islands. The kerf certificate runs with the clearance; the **no-core law** sweeps the kerf along the whole path out of the pocket (plus a wall ring) and refuses any piece not joined to the wall, by connectivity. At clearance = kerf offset the outer ring is the finished wall and the #532 corner minimum applies.\n- **sim** `verify::wire`: `WireJob.burnout` - the slug law reads a burnout as \"must free nothing\"; any freed piece is `WireFinding::Core`, blocking the post. Kerf and threading laws unchanged, so a ring that burns a wall blocks the post as a gouge.\n- **app**: `WireContourOp.burnout: Option<f64>` (seed `None`); `condition_of` refuses a clearance below the condition's kerf (CreateOperation and EditOperationParams, undoable); `generate_wire` branches; the stamp writes it only when set; `wire_verify` passes the flag. File mirror key `burnout_clearance` (absent = contour) - the MCP `edit_operation` params door patches that mirror, so it carries the field with no new tool.\n- **ui** `wire_page.rs`: Passes tab - \"Burn out the pocket (no core)\" and \"Wall clearance\".\n- **post**: no change - the burnout is one continuous threaded cut, so wire-iso.cps posts one thread / condition / comp-off before it and one cut / tip disposal after.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/540-wire-no-core.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/burnout_tests.rs`: `a_pocket_burns_out_with_no_core_left` (independent connectivity check: every piece the kerf leaves touches a wall), `a_clearance_below_the_kerf_is_refused_by_name`, `a_missing_or_misplaced_start_hole_and_a_punch_are_refused_by_name`, `a_pattern_that_cannot_reach_every_point_is_refused_by_name` (neck split; a single-ring path leaves a core), `at_the_kerf_offset_the_outer_ring_is_the_wall`.\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/wire/tests.rs`: `a_burnout_frees_nothing_and_a_core_is_refused`.\n- `crates/app/tests/wire_burnout.rs`: `the_burnout_posts_its_golden_with_no_slug` (new golden `tests/golden/nc/wire-iso/wire_burnout_pocket.nc`, through the gate with #534's laws), `a_clearance_below_the_kerf_is_refused_and_the_field_is_undoable` (command door, edit door, undo, file round trip), `a_burnout_pass_that_gouges_a_wall_blocks_the_post`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/534-wire-verify` green on the final head (sim, motion, app, ui suites); wire_post / wire_verify / wire_contour / wire_burnout by hand green; existing goldens byte-identical (wire_contour_punch.nc untouched, all app suites pass); clippy `-D warnings` on motion, sim, app, ui clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real EDM control (D10): the golden is on the synthetic fixture with invented `FX-...` codes.\n- An MCP round trip through the server (the door is the file mirror, tested by save/reopen).\n- Pockets with islands, or a raster/spiral pattern (refused / not offered; see the decision record).\n\n## Expected merges\n\nAdditive, but these edit the same lines: #539 (tabs) and #1150 (skims) both likely add fields to `WireContourOp` / `WireContourDto` / the stamp arm / `wire_page.rs` destructure / `WireJob` - keep both sides. #1150 also edits `posting_wire.rs` (untouched here).\n\nChangelog: Wire EDM no-core burnout - a Wire Contour can burn a closed pocket out by offset rings with a stated wall clearance, refusing a clearance under the kerf and any core left (#540)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #540\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
